   "text": "The drawing is a PROTAC. A spiro-oxindole MDM2-type ligand is joined through a benzamide, a piperidine and a PEG-type amine linker to a thalidomide unit.\n\n**Fragments, from left to right**\n- **Oxindole:** a 6-chloro-2-oxindole, spiro-fused at C3 to a pyrrolidine.\n- **Pyrrolidine:** its ring carbons carry the following.\n  - C2 has the carboxamide.\n  - C3 has a 3-chloro-2-fluorophenyl group.\n  - C4 is the spiro carbon shared with the oxindole.\n  - C5 is a second spiro carbon that closes a cyclohexane ring.\n  - The ring nitrogen is NH.\n- **Amide link:** the carboxamide nitrogen is attached to a para-phenylene, whose other end carries a C(=O) bonded to a piperidine nitrogen.\n- **Linker:** the piperidine 4-position bears an NH that continues as (CH2)3\u2013O\u2013(CH2)2\u2013O\u2013(CH2)2\u2013O\u2013(CH2)3\u2013NH.\n- **Thalidomide end:** that last NH is attached to C4 of the phthalimide ring. The phthalimide nitrogen bears a 2,6-dioxopiperidin-3-yl group, which is drawn without stereochemistry.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\n- Pyrrolidine C2 (hashed bond to the carboxamide): `[C@@H]`.\n- Pyrrolidine C3 (wedged bond to the aryl group): `[C@H]`.\n- Spiro C4 (hashed bond to the oxindole aromatic carbon, wedged bond to the oxindole C=O): `[C@]`.\n- The cyclohexane spiro carbon is not a stereocentre, since its two ring arms are identical.\n\nI assigned the @/@@ marks by working out the geometry from the wedge and hash bonds by hand, so they have not been checked with software.\n\nSMILES: O=C(Nc1ccc(cc1)C(=O)N1CCC(CC1)NCCCOCCOCCOCCCNc1cccc2c1C(=O)N(C1CCC(=O)NC1=O)C2=O)[C@@H]1NC2(CCCCC2)[C@]3([C@H]1c1cccc(Cl)c1F)C(=O)Nc1cc(Cl)ccc13"
  }
